    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41627": {
      "title": "Geomatics",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Part-Time Instructor | Geomatics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Part-Time Instructor | Geomatics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The Department of Built Environment invites applications for Part-Time Instructors for Spring 2027 and Fall 2027. Part-Time Instructors are temporary employees, hired on a semester-by-semester basis to teach courses for the Geomatics program. The successful candidate is expected to teach introductory and advanced-level courses for the Geomatics program. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: teaching face-to-face and/or online, attend training and/or review sessions. Additional duties will include, but are not limited to, academic advising, student organization support, participation in program development and assessment. The candidate will be expected to work cooperatively with faculty and staff in the department and university. We also welcome applications from qualified instructors who may not be able to be physically present on campus, where their teaching assignment and responsibilities can be appropriately supported through online delivery. Candidates must reside in North Carolina. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The Department of Built Environment supports over 290 undergraduate majors in the programs of Construction Management, Environmental Health and Safety and, Geomatics. The courses taught in the Geomatics program area are at the undergraduate level and can include Automated Surveying and Mapping, Residential Subdivision Design, Geodesy and Satellite Positioning (see below). https://www.ncat.edu/cost/departments/built-environment/academic-programs/geomatics/index.php N.C. A&T is a public, land-grant, doctoral research institution and has been the largest historically Black university in the country for the past decade. With an enrollment of 15,275 students in Fall 2026, the university offers 59 undergraduate degree programs, 36 master’s programs, and 12 doctoral programs. It is America’s top producer of Black graduates in Engineering and Agricultural Science bachelor’s programs, as well as a top five producer in numerous additional disciplines, including Liberal Arts and Communications/Journalism. It also ranks no. 3 in master’s degrees awarded to Black graduates in Engineering Technologies and Related Fields, no. 4 in master’s degrees in Engineering, and the no. 11 best business school for women in the nation. Nationally recognized for its leadership and excellence in STEM education and research, N.C. A&T is classified as “R2-High Research Activity” in the Carnegie Classifications and is poised to achieve “R1-Very High Research Activity” status. It also holds Carnegie’s earned credential in Community Engagement and the Association of Public and Land-Grant Universities ( APLU ) Innovation and Economic Prosperity designation. With an annual economic impact of $2.4 billion, N.C. A&T plays a vital role as a higher-education economic driver in North Carolina’s Piedmont Triad region and across a state that is ranked No. 1 in the nation for the second straight year as “best for business” by the CNBC financial network. Minimum Requirements Candidates must have a Master’s degree in the related discipline. Professional experience in Geomatics, Surveying, Civil Engineering, or a related field. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Relevant industry or teaching experience in one or more curriculum areas, including: AutoCAD Civil 3D, residential and subdivision design GNSS equipment and basic geodetic techniques Survey adjustment and measurements Photogrammetry and remote sensing Hydrology, Piping systems and related surveying/ GIS applications Practical industry experience and/or professional training in the assigned course area is an asset. Required License or Certification N/A Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Position Information Working Title Part-Time Instructor | Geomatics Position Number Recruitment Salary Range