      "title": "Student Success (Willie A. Deese College of Business &amp; Economics)",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Part Time Instructor | Student Success (Willie A. Deese College of Business &amp; Economics) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Part Time Instructor | Student Success (Willie A. Deese College of Business & Economics) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex - Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System (TSERS) Optional Supplemental Plans - 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The Willie A. Deese College of Business & Economics at North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University is seeking a dynamic and dedicated individual to join our team as a Part-Time Instructor. The selected candidate will be responsible for teaching student success and professional development courses as part of our student success colloquium. Courses may include Student Success Colloquium ( FRST 101, COBE 201, and/or COBE 301). This position offers an excellent opportunity to make a meaningful impact on students’ academic and professional journeys. Responsibilities: • Develop and deliver engaging and interactive course content focused on key skills for academic success, including time management, study strategies, goal setting, and academic planning. • Provide personalized guidance and support to students to help them navigate the college experience and achieve their academic and career/professional goals. • Cultivate a positive and inclusive learning environment that encourages student engagement and participation. • Monitor student progress and performance, offering timely feedback and support to promote student success. • Collaborate with fellow instructors and administrators to ensure the course effectively meets student needs and objectives. Part-time, temporary, flexible hours, with a potential course load of 3-6 credit hours. In person instruction. Part-Time Instructors are hired on a semester-by-semester basis. Primary Function of Organizational Unit N.C. A&T State University, is located in Greensboro, NC. An 1890 land-grant, doctoral, high research activity university, North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University prepares students to advance the human condition and facilitate economic growth in North Carolina and beyond by providing a preeminent and diverse educational experience through teaching, research and scholarly application of knowledge. The Willie A. Deese College of Business and Economics at North Carolina A&T State University has proudly maintained accreditation by the American Assembly of Collegiate Schools of Business ( AACSB International) since 1979. The Accounting accreditation has been in place since 1986. The most recent reaffirmation of accreditation occurred in fall 2021. The Deese College of Business and Economics is a thriving college with a new commitment that includes advancing graduate education, seeking opportunities to establish doctoral programs, advancing graduate education and research expansion. https://www.ncat.edu/cobe/index.php Minimum Requirements • Master’s degree in education, business, or a related field. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education • Previous teaching or mentoring experience, preferably in a higher education setting. • Knowledge of student success strategies and best practices in academic support. • Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. • Ability to effectively engage with a diverse student population. • Background in business, marketing, or entrepreneurship is encouraged. Required License or Certification Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Position Information Working Title Part Time Instructor | Student Success (Willie A. Deese College of Business & Economics) Position Number Recruitment Salary Range FLSA Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Part-time Tenure Track No FTE If Time Limited, Appointment Length Organizational Division Associate Dean's Office Organizational Location College of Business & Economics Organizational Unit Associate Dean's Office Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA3114 Open Date 06/19/2024 Close Date - for postings that do not use Open Until Filled Open Until Filled Yes Open Until Filled Minimum Application Period Postings: Positions remaining posted after this date are continuing to accept applications, but may close at any time. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration, applications received after this date may receive consideration depending upon the status of the search Date Position Available August 2026 Special Instructions to Applicant You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex – Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System ( TSERS ) Optional Supplemental Plans – 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/40742 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this employment opportunity: North Carolina A&T State University employment web page University of North Carolina System employment web page Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Education Research Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Listserv Other If you indicated you learned of this employment opportunity from an “Other” source please advise where you learned of the position: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Bachelor's Degree - Copy of transcripts Master's Degree - Copy of transcripts Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Ph.D. - Copy of transcripts Other Degree - Copy of transcripts Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be