Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex - Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System (TSERS) Optional Supplemental Plans - 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position This is a repost. Previous applicants need not re-apply for this temporary position. The Department of English invites applications for Part-Time Instructors for fall 2026. Part-Time Instructors are hired on a semester-by-semester basis to teach English courses. The successful candidate is expected to teach introductory and advanced level courses by the Department of English. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: teach face-to-face and/or online First-Year Composition ( FYC )/Humanities/Creative Writing courses, attend training and/or review sessions. Additional duties will include, but are not limited to, academic advising of students, supporting student organizations, participating in program development and assessment. The candidate will be expected to work cooperatively with faculty and staff in the department and university. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The English faculty comprises distinguished scholars and passionate teachers, who care about helping students become the intellectuals and leaders of tomorrow. This department teaches students how to think critically as well as how to understand and communicate in a diverse world. We have had graduates go into drama, law, mass media, politics and education. N.C. A&T’s Department of English offers an undergraduate major and minor and one graduate degree (M.A.). Through the College of Education students can also pursue a M.A.T in English Education . Students working towards a B.A. in English take a core of ten classes and then choose an area of concentration in African-American Literature, Creative Writing, English Literature or Technical Writing. A B.S. is offered in Undergraduate Teaching (Secondary Education). Our classes address a variety of innovative and traditional subjects, from literary surveys to focused examinations of subjects such as film, science fiction and hip-hop culture. https://www.ncat.edu/cahss/departments/english/index.php Minimum Requirements Candidates must have a Master’s degree in English or English Composition at time of application. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Candidates with 1-3 years teaching experience at the University or Community College level and with background in Rhetoric and Composition are preferred. Required License or Certification N/A Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Position Information Working Title Part-Time Instructor | English Position Number Recruitment Salary Range Commensurate with education and experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Part-time Tenure Track No FTE If Time Limited, Appointment Length Organizational Division English Dept Organizational Location College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Organizational Unit English Dept Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA1763 Open Date 04/01/2025 Close Date - for postings that do not use Open Until Filled Open Until Filled Yes Open Until Filled Minimum Application Period Postings: Positions remaining posted after this date are continuing to accept applications, but may close at any time. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration, applications received after this date may